b5ba394ae89e3c88d1a65","position":"1788322547824939001-aab19bf2-6c59-49df-9cb4-a60589ec1716"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"282e99fc4ba29ef91bdfc237b7e39601b7084b183fbfd8802ac9349045090a1e","event_uuid":"3b54ecb4-60fc-4473-b935-600c138e26e6","position":{"commit_sha":"ce5b77bf32df594f72a13234366477175930b3af","position":"1788322562817598001-3b54ecb4-60fc-4473-b935-600c138e26e6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"41c398941c226d94231776c6f50b777212cc1026da1cc21450f20edec69b8e83","event_uuid":"b0c4dff8-232d-4bf2-a570-8f6cc819c7b3","position":{"commit_sha":"ce5b77bf32df594f72a13234366477175930b3af","position":"1788322565118509001-b0c4dff8-232d-4bf2-a570-8f6cc819c7b3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-258_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b49fe82a-1778-4290-aefd-33d2684ae335","comments":[],"created_at":1788311553606421750,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\n56% of sampled fixes add a new mechanism (lock, knob, env var, gate script, fixture, helper, flag) vs 30% pure logic fixes (R2S1): the surface that produces future defect classes grows every fix cycle. No unified detector exists; per-kind precedents prove detectability (`check_config_reads.py`, `gen_env_registry.py`). Keyed per `(kind, name)`, never a scalar sum, so one kind cannot be traded against another.\n\n## Approach\n\n`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` detects, per repo STATE (state-diffing the baseline is simpler than diffing a change and equivalent), seven mechanism kinds.\n\n**The kinds PARTITION the surface: every definition site yields exactly ONE `(kind, name)` entry.** This is correctness, not tidiness, and it constrains BOTH the kind assignment and the name.\n\n*Kind.* A boolean `rebar.toml` key would otherwise be counted twice — once as `config_key`, once as `feature_flag` — because the flag detector reads the same `_SECTIONS` dict, so one site would need two justifications and a per-kind marker could not express that. `feature_flag` therefore claims the boolean-coerced entries and `config_key` claims only the non-boolean remainder.\n\n*Name.* `config_key` and `feature_flag` names are **section-qualified** as `<section>.<key>`. `_SECTIONS` repeats key names across sections — `allow_insecure` is `_as_bool` in BOTH `reconciler` and `jira` (`_config_sections.py:140`, `:151`) — so a bare name collapses two definition sites into one entry: removing one while the other persists shows no delta, and a third same-named key is admitted silently. AC1 is tested against the qualified name.\n\nLive counts, locked at introduction:\n\n| kind | detection | count |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lock` | AST `ClassDef` `.*Lock.*` + literals matching `\\.lock$` | 26 |\n| `env_var` | `gen_env_registry.scan()`, `REBAR_*` only | 132 |\n| `config_key` | `_SECTIONS` non-boolean, named `<section>.<key>` | 76 |\n| `feature_flag` | `_SECTIONS` boolean, named `<section>.<key>` | 27 |\n| `ci_gate` | `scripts/check_*.py` + workflow `run:` steps | 280 (29 + 251) |\n| `autouse_fixture` | AST `pytest.fixture(autouse=True)` | 145 |\n| `test_helper` | `tests/_*.py` glob | 19 |\n\n**Baseline and modes.** `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, shape `{\"schema_version\": 1, \"mechanisms\": {\"<kind>::<name>\": 1}}`, sorted keys, duplicate-member and UTF-8 rejection — a port of the complexity baseline's validated schema, whose four-bucket `compare()` and `has_regression` port unchanged.\n\nAdopts `--check` and `--update-stale`; omits the complexity gate's third mode `--lock`, which exists only because that threshold is administrator-locked. The mechanism baseline has no locked limit, so `--lock` would guard nothing.\n\n**The justified-exception path is an in-tree marker parsed by this script**, exactly as `check_config_reads.py` consumes its own `# read-via:` markers:\n\n```\n# mechanism-ok: <kind> <name> — <reason or ticket id>\n```\n\nA blank reason is itself an error. Because the kinds partition, one site needs one marker naming one kind.\n\n**Where the marker attaches.** Three kinds are detected by filename glob or YAML structure and have no definition line, so placement is stated per detection shape; each detector scans exactly these locations:\n\n| detection shape | kinds | marker location |\n|---|---|---|\n| Python definition line | `lock` class, `autouse_fixture`, `config_key`, `feature_flag` | that line, or the one before it |\n| string literal | `lock` filenames, `env_var` | the literal's line or the one before it, in any attributed file |\n| filename glob | `ci_gate` scripts, `test_helper` | the matched file's first 20 lines |\n| YAML step | `ci_gate` workflow `run:` steps | the step's `- name:`/`run:` line or the one before it |\n\nA mechanism attributed to several files is admitted by a marker in any one; the diagnostic names every attributed file.\n\n(An earlier draft routed justification through the DET floor. That was wrong: `det_floor.py` is the per-ticket plan-review gate, is not in `make lint`, and cannot be consulted by a tree-scanning script.)\n\n**Both repo limit-gates scan `src/rebar` only** (`module_size_support` walks `SRC_ROOT`; the ratchet sets `PRODUCTION_SCOPE`), while everything here ships under `scripts/`. Neither measures this code, so AC15/AC16 assert the limits in this ticket's own suite.\n\n**Structure.** Ships as `scripts/_mechanism_delta/{baseline,compare,detect_code,detect_config,detect_ci}.py` with a thin entrypoint — seven detectors in one file would breach both limits. Detectors split by INPUT SURFACE (AST / config registry / globs+YAML); dispatch is a flat `{kind: callable}` table. Portable: stdlib plus PyYAML, triggered by `make lint`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: the seven detectors' name sets are pairwise disjoint on the current tree. Verified by a test asserting every pair has an empty intersection.\n- [ ] AC2: `config_key` excludes boolean-coerced `_SECTIONS` entries. Verified by a test asserting its live count is 76.\n- [ ] AC3: `feature_flag` claims exactly those boolean entries. Verified by a test asserting its live count is 27.\n- [ ] AC4: the script detects all seven kinds with zero false positives. Verified by `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exiting 0 on a clean tree.\n- [ ] AC5: `--check` exits non-zero when a new `(kind, name)` appears unjustified. Verified by a parameterized test seeding one new mechanism of each of the seven kinds.\n- [ ] AC6: a valid marker admits a new mechanism of a definition-line kind. Verified by a test seeding a marked `_SECTIONS` entry.\n- [ ] AC7: a valid marker admits a filename-glob kind. Verified by a test seeding a new `scripts/check_*.py` with its marker in the first 20 lines.\n- [ ] AC8: a valid marker admits a YAML-step kind. Verified by a test seeding a workflow `run:` step with a marker on the preceding line.\n- [ ] AC9: a blank-reason marker fails. Verified by a test seeding one.\n- [ ] AC10: mechanism removal passes. Verified by a test removing a baselined mechanism and asserting exit 0.\n- [ ] AC11: `--update-stale` refuses to write when `new>0` or `increased>0`. Verified by a test asserting the refusal and that the baseline is byte-identical afterwards.\n- [ ] AC12: `make lint` runs the check. Verified by a test asserting the `lint` target contains the invocation.\n- [ ] AC13: the ratchet and its seven kinds are documented beside the complexity ratchet. Verified by a test asserting the docs name all seven kind identifiers.\n- [ ] AC14: the marker placement table is documented in that section. Verified by a test asserting the docs name each of the four detection shapes.\n- [ ] AC15: every shipped module stays under the 800-LOC cap. Verified by a test asserting each shipped file's line count against `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n- [ ] AC16: every shipped function stays under the complexity-15 ceiling. Verified by a test running `ruff check --select C901` over the shipped `scripts/` files and asserting no finding.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py -v` — covers AC1–AC3 and AC5–AC16. Census counts are derived LIVE from the tree, never hardcoded, following `test_complexity_baseline.py`'s stated discipline.\n- `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` — exits 0 on the clean tree (AC4).\n- `make lint` / `make typecheck` — the gate runs in place (AC12) and the package type-checks.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` — entrypoint plus dispatch table\n- `scripts/_mechanism_delta/` — `baseline`, `compare`, `detect_code`, `detect_config`, `detect_ci`\n- `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` — locked at introduction\n- `Makefile` — lint wiring after `check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n- `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` — the precedent `test_complexity_baseline.py` is in `tests/unit/`\n- `docs/` — ratchet note beside the complexity ratchet","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py","reason":"entrypoint + flat kind->detector dispatch table"},{"path":"scripts/_mechanism_delta/baseline.py","reason":"schema/parse/render/write, ported from the complexity baseline"},{"path":"scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py","reason":"four-bucket compare + violation rendering"},{"path":"scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_code.py","reason":"AST detectors: locks, autouse fixtures, tests/_*.py helpers"},{"path":"scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py","reason":"env vars, config keys, feature flags"},{"path":"scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_ci.py","reason":"check_*.py scripts + workflow run: steps"},{"path":".github/mechanism-baseline.json","reason":"per-(kind,name) baseline locked at introduction"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"lint wiring after check_complexity_baseline.py --check"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py","reason":"per-kind seeded fire, marker pass/fail, shrink semantics, Makefile wiring"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","87cb-7121-a3b6-4606"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"87cb-7121-a3b6-4606","parent_status_uuid":"3b54ecb4-60fc-4473-b935-600c138e26e6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9ca8-675e-4dfb-427d","ticket_type":"story","title":"Deterministic mechanism-delta ratchet: check_mechanism_delta.py with per-(kind,name) shrink-only baseline","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5ed3455b-d308-431b-874d-dbe59bfa7072","da7b38cd-6edc-46a3-ab97-107d083b4c0e","ec7a079e-b348-4130-8ca9-fb106c78ba35","938c3187-154a-434a-80ac-5a458bea1e0f","42b4c96b-ede3-44d8-8c64-95ee5c3a7cd0","16f913b4-f21d-40fd-a61a-280bb3b2644f","26bf991d-cc0b-49fc-b585-2db085df1b07","3c1ceb3e-4784-4aeb-8d97-9661074fed74","62e3927d-8ca4-477b-97f3-7f8b315f3bfc","1f28ae4e-e6ba-4032-97c6-ff0b940c30d8","fbc8bd3c-fe4e-42a7-8d0b-0e6c8ea68c6e","60e1cf73-beba-49ee-b636-95b86f56eed6","7fadf61e-b905-4ca4-ac3c-cf9cc681b817","aab19bf2-6c59-49df-9cb4-a60589ec1716","3b54ecb4